  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 is the clear current best (0.653 acc, config_006), with aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) making negligible difference. Image-only with resnet50 is very weak (0.208), raising the question of whether image features can add complementary signal when fused with the strong RNA representation. The biggest open uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion can push beyond the 0.653 RNA-only ceiling. This experiment tests that directly: it pairs the best-validated RNA configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) with the already-characterized resnet50 image encoder and uses simple concat fusion. By holding the image encoder to resnet50 (the only one we've seen), we isolate the fusion question without confounding with an untested image backbone. If multimodal helps, the next step is to try ViT-L; if it does not, we learn that image features (at least at this quality level) are not complementary to the RNA signal, redirecting effort toward RNA-side improvements. This is the highest-information next experiment under the limited budget."
}

